module contract;

// CFL wall-clock reading — resource-projection vocabulary version 1.
//
// Card W37-CORPUS-CONTRACTS-4. ONE TRUSTED ASSUMPTION about one upstream
// function. This module verifies nothing: the C body is not analyzed by this
// loader, and a declaration is a premise.
//
// Read from the pinned checkout at Fluent Bit
// 66910c10a4d7eafa810b84229cf2dcf7b0f26f97 on this card's own run.
//
// ## Why this callee
//
// `cfl_time_now` is the SOLE blocker of one projected function, `ctr_span_end`
// (`lib/ctraces/src/ctr_span.c:268-274`), whose single leaf is the call at
// `:272`.
//
// ## The body, read from `lib/cfl/src/cfl_time.c:31-60`
//
//     uint64_t cfl_time_now()
//     {
//         struct timespec tm = {0};
//         ...
//     #if defined CFL_HAVE_CLOCK_GET_TIME        /* macOS */
//         clock_serv_t cclock;
//         mach_timespec_t mts;
//         host_get_clock_service(mach_host_self(), CALENDAR_CLOCK, &cclock);
//         clock_get_time(cclock, &mts);
//         tm.tv_sec = mts.tv_sec;
//         tm.tv_nsec = mts.tv_nsec;
//         mach_port_deallocate(mach_task_self(), cclock);
//     #elif defined CFL_HAVE_TIMESPEC_GET        /* C11 */
//         timespec_get(&tm, TIME_UTC);
//     #else
//         clock_gettime(CLOCK_REALTIME, &tm);
//     #endif
//
//         return (((uint64_t) tm.tv_sec * 1000000000L) + tm.tv_nsec);
//     }
//
//   * The function takes NO PARAMETERS, so there is no custody to state on the
//     way in. It is the simplest possible custody-neutral declaration.
//   * The only object it touches is `tm`, a function-LOCAL `struct timespec`
//     whose address is passed to a clock call and which does not outlive the
//     call. Nothing is allocated, nothing is released, nothing is stored.
//   * The result is `uint64_t`, a SCALAR nanosecond count. A scalar result
//     carries no custody, so `resource_return_none()` is the faithful — and the
//     only writable — result mode; v1's owning result modes require a pointer
//     return type.
//   * On the macOS arm a mach port is acquired and released within the body
//     (`host_get_clock_service` / `mach_port_deallocate`); it is balanced there
//     and never reaches the caller. The audited targets take the
//     `clock_gettime`/`timespec_get` arm in any case, and this declaration
//     states the same custody fact on every arm: none crosses the boundary.
//
// ## The unprototyped `()` declaration, and why it is settled by precedent
//
// The header spells the function with an EMPTY parameter list rather than
// `(void)`:
//
//     lib/cfl/include/cfl/cfl_time.h:25
//         uint64_t cfl_time_now();
//
// which in C is an unprototyped declaration with unspecified parameters, not a
// declaration of arity zero. Whether constraint 8's arity gate accepts a
// zero-arity contract against it is a real question, and it is NOT left to
// hope: the corpus already declares `flb_time_now`, whose C declaration is the
// SAME shape —
//
//     include/fluent-bit/flb_lib.h:94
//         FLB_EXPORT double flb_time_now();
//
// — as a zero-arity contract in `contract/qcore/fluent_bit/time.qcore`, and it
// is manifest-selected and not withdrawn in the pinned corpus. So this shape is
// exercised production text, measured rather than assumed, and this declaration
// follows it exactly.
//
// ## Defined in no analysed unit
//
// `lib/cfl/src/cfl_time.c` is NOT among the 185 analysed units, so constraint
// 8's duty gate has no derived summary to compare against and nothing here can
// be withdrawn on a body this corpus does not define. Checked against the
// baseline's own unit list.
//
// ## ABI (constraint 8)
//
// One definition in the whole tree, external linkage. `uint64_t` projects to
// `u64` under the LP64 model of the audited targets (`LOADER-ABI-LP64`).
//
// ## NOT CLAIMED
//
// Nothing about the clock: not its resolution, not its monotonicity, not its
// epoch, not whether the underlying `clock_gettime`/`timespec_get` succeeded —
// this body discards that status, which is an upstream fact this declaration
// neither endorses nor reports. This is the same sentence
// `fluent_bit/time.qcore` writes about `flb_time_now`, for the same reason. A
// custody declaration says what happens to the caller's resources, and this one
// says: nothing.
//
// ## Read at the same time and DELIBERATELY LEFT UNDECLARED
//
// `cfl_time_to_nanosec` and the rest of the `cfl_time_*` family block no
// projected function in the baseline. `timespec_get`, `clock_gettime`,
// `host_get_clock_service`, `clock_get_time`, `mach_host_self`,
// `mach_task_self` and `mach_port_deallocate` are named by this body and are
// undeclared for the same reason.

// --- the wall-clock reading ctraces timestamps a span's end with ---
extern fn cfl_time_now() -> u64
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};
